er investor demand fell short. It will now cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering, utility-capex-2027). So the equity shortfall is already reducing spending.\n- **Sector:** Equity markets have been less receptive, and two utility share offerings were cut back in size (utility-credit). The sector looks weak for equity, not just Pellham.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It plans 2027 capex up 12%. It priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so debt is its working route, not equity.\n- **Debt:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, so debt is open but more expensive.\n\n**Implication:** Capex that depends on equity, as Pellham's does, is at risk of being cut or deferred. Capex that can be funded with debt, as Norvane's can, looks more secure. For suppliers of grid equipment, Pellham's equity failure is a downside risk to 2027 transformer demand. My sources don't show when equity conditions might improve.","ttft_ms":2135,"type":"result","duration_ms":14335,"uuid":"447540e3-5fc2-4292-9550-2f8f6218cf69","ttft_stream_ms":1134,"time_to_request_ms":82,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":13,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":21,"input_attachments":7,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":32,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":71,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":182,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":108,"process_rss_mib_result":192,"process_anon_mib_result":112,"process_peak_rss_mib":192,"process_cpu_ms_turn":464,"process_wall_ms_turn":14334,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1